# HLD Phase Executor Workflow
# Orchestration template for systematic HLD execution with TDD and phase gates

# ===== PHASE 0: HLD PARSING & SETUP =====

# Parse the HLD document and extract phases
general-purpose:"Parse the HLD document provided by the user. Extract all phases with their names, descriptions, deliverables, dependencies, validation criteria, and deployment commands. Build a dependency graph (DAG) and verify no circular dependencies exist. Create the initial state tracker at .agent/hld-execution-state.md":hld_parsed ->

# User approval of parsed structure
@approve-hld-structure ->

# ===== PHASE EXECUTION LOOP =====
# Note: This is a template - actual execution iterates through phases

# Identify next executable phase
general-purpose:"Read .agent/hld-execution-state.md. Identify the next phase that: (1) has status 'pending', (2) has all dependencies marked 'complete', (3) has all dependency validation gates passed. If no phase is executable, report blocked status.":next_phase_identified ->

# Check if work remains
(if next_phase_identified.has_pending_phases)~>

# ===== PER-PHASE TDD CYCLE =====

# Generate mini TDD plan for the phase
general-purpose:"For the identified phase, transform its deliverables into a TDD plan with: (1) Master goals from deliverables, (2) Exit criteria from validation criteria, (3) RED-GREEN-REFACTOR phases. Write plan to .agent/phase-N-tdd-plan.md and update scratchpad.":phase_tdd_plan_generated ->

# Execute RED phase - write failing tests
general-purpose:"Execute RED phase: Write failing tests for each deliverable. Each test must: (1) clearly test one deliverable, (2) fail with meaningful error, (3) fail due to missing implementation not test errors. Verify all tests fail before proceeding.":red_phase_complete ->

# Verify RED phase
general-purpose:"Run test suite and confirm all new tests fail as expected. Document which tests were written and their failure reasons in the execution log.":red_verified ->

# Execute GREEN phase - minimal implementation
general-purpose:"Execute GREEN phase: Write minimal code to make all tests pass. Do not add features beyond what tests require. Do not refactor yet. Focus on making tests green.":green_phase_complete ->

# Verify GREEN phase
general-purpose:"Run test suite and confirm all tests pass. Ensure no regressions in existing tests. Document implementation summary in execution log.":green_verified ->

# Execute REFACTOR phase
[
  general-purpose:"Execute REFACTOR phase: Clean up implementation. Remove duplication, improve naming, extract helpers. Keep all tests passing throughout.":refactoring_complete ||

  general-purpose:"Apply code simplifier and review tools. Check for complexity issues and address them while maintaining test coverage.":code_review_complete
] ->

# Verify REFACTOR phase
general-purpose:"Run full test suite after refactoring. Verify all tests still pass and coverage has not decreased.":refactor_verified ->

# ===== PHASE VALIDATION GATE =====

# Run parallel validation checks
[
  general-purpose:"Run unit tests: npm test. Capture results and any failures.":unit_tests_result ||

  general-purpose:"Run build and lint: npm run build && npm run lint. Capture results.":build_lint_result ||

  general-purpose:"Run security review using /security-review and /security-scanning:security-sast. Capture findings.":security_result
] ->

# Run deployment validation (if deployment command specified)
general-purpose:"If phase has deployment command, execute it. Capture deployment output and verify success. If no deployment command, skip this step.":deployment_result ->

# Run integration tests (if specified)
general-purpose:"If phase has integration test command, execute it. Capture results. If no integration tests, skip this step.":integration_result ->

# Compile validation results
general-purpose:"Compile all validation results into a summary. Determine if phase validation passed (all checks green) or failed (any check red). Prepare summary for user review.":validation_summary ->

# User checkpoint for phase approval
@phase-validation-gate ->

# ===== PHASE COMPLETION =====

# Mark phase complete
general-purpose:"Update .agent/hld-execution-state.md: (1) Mark current phase as 'complete', (2) Record validation results, (3) Update dependency graph to unblock dependent phases, (4) Create git tag 'hld-phase-N-complete', (5) Commit phase changes.":phase_marked_complete ->

# Check for more phases
general-purpose:"Check if all phases are complete. If yes, proceed to final summary. If no, loop back to identify next phase.":completion_check ->

# Conditional: more phases to execute
(if completion_check.phases_remaining)~> next_phase_identified ||

# ===== FINAL SUMMARY =====

# Generate completion report
general-purpose:"Generate final HLD execution report: (1) List all completed phases with timestamps, (2) Summarize validation results, (3) List any skipped phases or known issues, (4) Provide cleanup recommendations.":final_report ->

@hld-execution-complete
